    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d712">

                <pb facs="0704" n="1438" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1438"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-02"><hi rendition="#italic">January 2,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your 725 shows that promised protection was not given to American citizens at
                    Cæsarea until danger was virtually over. Represent this <pb facs="0705" n="1439"
                        xml:id="pg1439"/> strongly, and ask signal rebuke of delinquent officer and
                    peremptory orders for instant protection in any threatened quarter at the first
                    sign of disturbance. The assurances of the Porte must be supported in fact in
                    order to satisfy this Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
